.TH mergecps "1" "" "The scalpel3 Checkpoint Merger" "The scalpel3 Checkpoint Merger"

.SH NAME
mergecps \- Merge scalpel3 checkpoint directories

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mergecps
\fIcheckpoint_dir1\fR
\fIcheckpoint_dir2\fR
\fIoutput_dir\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBmergecps\fR combines two scalpel3 checkpoint directories into a single
output directory after windowed carving, allowing a subsequent
\fBscalpel3 -R\fR invocation to resume from the merged state. Stop both
input runs before merging.
.PP
Inputs must use the same scalpel3 executable, image and blockmap pathnames,
block size, file type mapping, and block validation dispositions. The stored
blockmap pathname must still be readable. Use runs with compatible recovery
settings; settings not explicitly merged are taken from the first input.
.PP
Each input checkpoint directory must contain the persistent
\fIblockclassification.dat\fR created when block validation completed.
For each input, \fBmergecps\fR verifies the published checkpoint slot and
falls back to the newest other valid slot if necessary.  It never combines
files from different generations of one input checkpoint.
.PP
\fBmergecps\fR validates and merges the classification tables and writes a
new \fIblockclassification.dat\fR with a new two-slot checkpoint in the
output directory.  The output directory must not already exist.  The complete
result is first written to a temporary sibling directory and is atomically
published only after its checkpoint manifest and current-slot marker are
durable.
.PP
Distinct clone candidates and the saved validator state belonging to each
retained candidate are preserved. If both inputs contain the same candidate
(the same primary and clone UUIDs), the first input's candidate and its state
take precedence. Saved block state is combined, with the first input taking
precedence for a duplicate block-state key.
.PP
This command does not merge or copy recovered payloads, audit logs, or the
external image blockmap. Retain the original output directories and combine
blockmap coverage separately with \fBmergeblockmap\fR(1) when needed.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and nonzero if the checkpoints are incompatible,
invalid, or cannot be read or written.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scalpel3 (1),
.BR mergeblockmap (1)

.SH AUTHOR
Golden G. Richard III.
